IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`
IMPORT `ccc13-fares-minerals`
IMPORT `ccc13-tests-support`

-- ccc13-tests-fares-minerals.l4 -- tests of ccc13-fares-minerals.l4 (ss 393 to 396). Expected values are decided from the text.

`ccc13 test the hybrid class` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
GIVETH A `s 2 valuable mineral kind`
`ccc13 test a precious metal` MEANS `a precious metal`
GIVETH A `s 2 valuable mineral kind`
`ccc13 test a mineral` MEANS `a mineral`
GIVETH A `s 2 valuable mineral kind`
`ccc13 test not a valuable mineral` MEANS `a thing that is none of those`

§ `s 393 fraud in relation to fares`
-- inputs of (1): duty to collect; intentionally; (a) fails to collect; (b) collects less; (c) accepts consideration
#ASSERT `s 393(1) the conduct is the offence of fraud in relation to fares by the person who collects them` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 393(1) the conduct is the offence of fraud in relation to fares by the person who collects them` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 393(1) the conduct is the offence of fraud in relation to fares by the person who collects them` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 393(1) the conduct is the offence of fraud in relation to fares by the person who collects them` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- no duty to collect
#ASSERT `s 393(1) the conduct is the offence of fraud in relation to fares by the person who collects them` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE      -- not intentionally
#ASSERT `s 393(1) the conduct is the offence of fraud in relation to fares by the person who collects them` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- none of (a), (b), (c)
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`s 393(1) the punishments` `ccc13 test p787`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`
#ASSERT `s 393(1) the class of the offence` EQUALS `ccc13 test the hybrid class`
#ASSERT `s 393(2) the conduct is the offence of giving or offering consideration to the person who collects fares` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 393(2) the conduct is the offence of giving or offering consideration to the person who collects fares` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 393(2) the conduct is the offence of giving or offering consideration to the person who collects fares` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 393(2) the conduct is the offence of giving or offering consideration to the person who collects fares` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`s 393(2) the punishments` `ccc13 test p787`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `two years`
#ASSERT `s 393(2) the class of the offence` EQUALS `ccc13 test the hybrid class`
#ASSERT `s 393(3) the conduct is the offence of fraudulently obtaining transportation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 393(3) the conduct is the offence of fraudulently obtaining transportation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 393(3) the conduct is the offence of fraudulently obtaining transportation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- subsection (3) is summary only: one limb, the s 787(1) answer, and no indictable limb
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the number of limbs` (`s 393(3) the punishments` `ccc13 test p787`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the summary limb is the s 787(1) stand-in` (`s 393(3) the punishments` `ccc13 test p787`) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`s 393(3) the punishments` `ccc13 test p787`) EQUALS `no imprisonment is stated`
#ASSERT `s 393(3) the class of the offence` EQUALS `an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `s 394 fraud in relation to valuable minerals`
-- inputs of (1): holder; fraudulent device; defrauded of minerals; defrauded of money; conceals; kind of mineral; value per kilogram
#ASSERT `s 394(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `ccc13 test a precious metal` 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE       -- (a)(i)
#ASSERT `s 394(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `ccc13 test a precious metal` 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE       -- (a)(ii)
#ASSERT `s 394(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `ccc13 test a precious metal` 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE      -- (b)
#ASSERT `s 394(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `ccc13 test a precious metal` 1 EQUALS NOTHING        -- not the holder: outside the prohibition
#ASSERT `s 394(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `ccc13 test not a valuable mineral` 0 EQUALS NOTHING   -- (a)(i) needs a valuable mineral
#ASSERT `s 394(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `ccc13 test a mineral` 99 EQUALS NOTHING              -- a mineral under $100 a kilogram is not a valuable mineral
#ASSERT `s 394(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE `ccc13 test a mineral` 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE             -- at $100 a kilogram it is
#ASSERT `s 394(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `ccc13 test not a valuable mineral` 0 EQUALS JUST TRUE   -- (a)(ii) does not turn on the mineral
#ASSERT `s 394(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `ccc13 test a precious metal` 1 EQUALS NOTHING         -- no act of (a) or (b)
-- inputs of (2): sells; unprocessed; is the owner, the owner's agent or someone acting under lawful authority; kind; value
#ASSERT `s 394(2) the person contravenes subsection (2)` TRUE TRUE FALSE `ccc13 test a precious metal` 500 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 394(2) the person contravenes subsection (2)` TRUE TRUE TRUE `ccc13 test a precious metal` 500 EQUALS NOTHING        -- the owner or an agent: "other than the owner"
#ASSERT `s 394(2) the person contravenes subsection (2)` FALSE TRUE FALSE `ccc13 test a precious metal` 500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 394(2) the person contravenes subsection (2)` TRUE FALSE FALSE `ccc13 test a precious metal` 500 EQUALS NOTHING       -- refined and processed
#ASSERT `s 394(2) the person contravenes subsection (2)` TRUE TRUE FALSE `ccc13 test a mineral` 99 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 394(2) the person contravenes subsection (2)` TRUE TRUE FALSE `ccc13 test a mineral` 100 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- inputs of (3): buys; unprocessed; reason to believe the seller is not the owner; kind; value
#ASSERT `s 394(3) the person contravenes subsection (3)` TRUE TRUE TRUE `ccc13 test a precious metal` 500 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 394(3) the person contravenes subsection (3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE `ccc13 test a precious metal` 500 EQUALS NOTHING       -- no reason to believe
#ASSERT `s 394(3) the person contravenes subsection (3)` FALSE TRUE TRUE `ccc13 test a precious metal` 500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 394(3) the person contravenes subsection (3)` TRUE FALSE TRUE `ccc13 test a precious metal` 500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 394(3) the person contravenes subsection (3)` TRUE TRUE TRUE `ccc13 test not a valuable mineral` 500 EQUALS NOTHING
-- the presumptions: the proceeding is in relation to subsection (2) or (3); evidence raising a reasonable doubt
#ASSERT `s 394(4)(a) it is presumed, in the case of a sale, that the seller is not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 394(4)(a) it is presumed, in the case of a sale, that the seller is not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- evidence raising a reasonable doubt
#ASSERT `s 394(4)(a) it is presumed, in the case of a sale, that the seller is not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE   -- not a proceeding in relation to subsection (2)
#ASSERT `s 394(4)(b) it is presumed, in the case of a purchase, that the purchaser had reason to believe that the seller was not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 394(4)(b) it is presumed, in the case of a purchase, that the purchaser had reason to believe that the seller was not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 394(4)(b) it is presumed, in the case of a purchase, that the purchaser had reason to believe that the seller was not the owner or the owner's agent or someone otherwise acting under lawful authority` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (5): guilty when any of (1), (2), (3) is contravened
#ASSERT `s 394(5) the person is guilty of an offence for contravening subsection (1), (2) or (3)` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 394(5) the person is guilty of an offence for contravening subsection (1), (2) or (3)` NOTHING NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 394(5) the person is guilty of an offence for contravening subsection (1), (2) or (3)` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING             -- none contravened: the prohibitions are limited by their own wording
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`s 394(5) the punishments` `ccc13 test p787`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`
#ASSERT `s 394(5) the class of the offence` EQUALS `ccc13 test the hybrid class`
-- (6), (7) forfeiture
#ASSERT `s 394(6) the court may order the thing forfeited to Her Majesty` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 394(6) the court may order the thing forfeited to Her Majesty` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING         -- not convicted: "If a person is convicted" is a gate on a power (fork F7)
#ASSERT `s 394(6) the court may order the thing forfeited to Her Majesty` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 394(7) subsection (6) does not apply to the thing` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE                  -- real property not built or modified for the purpose
#ASSERT `s 394(7) subsection (6) does not apply to the thing` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE                  -- real property built or modified for the purpose: outside the exception
#ASSERT `s 394(7) subsection (6) does not apply to the thing` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING                   -- not real property: the exception is silent
#ASSERT `s 394(6) the court may order the thing forfeited, subject to subsection (7)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 394(6) the court may order the thing forfeited, subject to subsection (7)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 394(6) the court may order the thing forfeited, subject to subsection (7)` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 394(6) the court may order the thing forfeited, subject to subsection (7)` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#TRACE `s 394(6) the power of the court` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 394(6) order the thing forfeited to Her Majesty` AT 1
#TRACE `s 394(6) the power of the court` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
#TRACE `s 394(6) the power of the court` NOTHING AT 0 WITH

§ `s 394.1 possession of stolen or fraudulently obtained valuable minerals`
-- inputs of (1): possesses; unprocessed; stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394; kind; value
#ASSERT `s 394.1(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE TRUE `ccc13 test a precious metal` 500 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 394.1(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` FALSE TRUE TRUE `ccc13 test a precious metal` 500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 394.1(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE FALSE TRUE `ccc13 test a precious metal` 500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 394.1(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE FALSE `ccc13 test a precious metal` 500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 394.1(1) the person contravenes subsection (1)` TRUE TRUE TRUE `ccc13 test a mineral` 99 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 394.1(2) the reasonable grounds are proof that the valuable mineral has been stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 394.1(2) the reasonable grounds are proof that the valuable mineral has been stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 394.1(2) the reasonable grounds are proof that the valuable mineral has been stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 394.1(3) the person is guilty of an offence for contravening subsection (1)` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 394.1(3) the person is guilty of an offence for contravening subsection (1)` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`s 394.1(3) the punishments` `ccc13 test p787`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `five years`
#ASSERT `s 394.1(3) the class of the offence` EQUALS `ccc13 test the hybrid class`
#ASSERT `s 394.1(4) the court may order the thing forfeited to Her Majesty` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 394.1(4) the court may order the thing forfeited to Her Majesty` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 394.1(4) the court may order the thing forfeited to Her Majesty` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 394.1(5) subsection (4) does not apply to the thing` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 394.1(5) subsection (4) does not apply to the thing` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 394.1(5) subsection (4) does not apply to the thing` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 394.1(4) the court may order the thing forfeited, subject to subsection (5)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 394.1(4) the court may order the thing forfeited, subject to subsection (5)` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#TRACE `s 394.1(4) the power of the court` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `s 394.1(4) order the thing forfeited to Her Majesty` AT 1

§ `s 395 search for valuable minerals`
-- inputs of (1): information laid under oath; informant is a peace officer (s 2); informant is a public officer (s 2); appointed or designated, duties include enforcement; justice satisfied
#ASSERT `s 395(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a search for valuable minerals` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE          -- a peace officer
#ASSERT `s 395(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a search for valuable minerals` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE          -- a qualifying public officer
#ASSERT `s 395(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a search for valuable minerals` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING            -- a public officer not appointed or designated
#ASSERT `s 395(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a search for valuable minerals` FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING           -- no information laid under oath
#ASSERT `s 395(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a search for valuable minerals` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING           -- the justice is not satisfied
#ASSERT `s 395(1) the justice may issue a warrant authorizing a search for valuable minerals` TRUE NOTHING (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING               -- s 2 peace officer is NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 395(1) the warrant authorizes the officer to search` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 395(1) the warrant authorizes the officer to search` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 395(1) the warrant authorizes the officer to search` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING       -- a public officer not named in the warrant
#ASSERT `s 395(1.1) the warrant may be executed at the place` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 395(1.1) the warrant may be executed at the place` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 395(1.1) the officer who executes the warrant has the authority the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 395(1.1) the officer who executes the warrant has the authority the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 395(1.1) the officer who executes the warrant has the authority the subsection requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 395(2) the thing found shall be seized and brought before a justice` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 395(2) the thing found shall be seized and brought before a justice` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 395(2) the order the justice shall make` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 395(2)(a) that it be detained for the purposes of an inquiry or a trial`
#ASSERT `s 395(2) the order the justice shall make` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 395(2)(a) that it be detained for the purposes of an inquiry or a trial`
#ASSERT `s 395(2) the order the justice shall make` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 395(2)(b)(i) that it be restored to the owner`
#ASSERT `s 395(2) the order the justice shall make` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 395(2)(b)(ii) that it be forfeited to Her Majesty in right of the province in which the proceedings take place`
#TRACE `s 395(2) the duty of the justice` `s 395(2)(b)(i) that it be restored to the owner` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a justice` DOES `s 395(2) order that it be restored to the owner` AT 1
#TRACE `s 395(2) the duty of the justice` `s 395(2)(a) that it be detained for the purposes of an inquiry or a trial` AT 0 WITH
#ASSERT `s 395(3) an appeal lies from the order` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 395(3) an appeal lies from the order` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING     -- an order under paragraph (2)(a) is not mentioned

§ `s 396 offences in relation to mines`
-- inputs: (a) adds to or removes from a mine, claim or oil well; (b) adds, removes or tampers with a sample; fraudulent intent to affect the result
#ASSERT `s 396(1) the conduct is the offence of interfering with a mine or its samples` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 396(1) the conduct is the offence of interfering with a mine or its samples` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 396(1) the conduct is the offence of interfering with a mine or its samples` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 396(1) the conduct is the offence of interfering with a mine or its samples` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE     -- no fraudulent intent
#ASSERT `ccc13 test the maximum imprisonment by indictment` (`s 396(1) the punishments` `ccc13 test p787`) EQUALS `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`
#ASSERT `s 396(1) the class of the offence` EQUALS `ccc13 test the hybrid class`
-- inputs of (2): proceedings under (1); evidence of an addition, removal or tampering; evidence to the contrary
#ASSERT `s 396(2) the evidence is proof of a fraudulent intent to affect the result of an assay, a test or a valuation` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 396(2) the evidence is proof of a fraudulent intent to affect the result of an assay, a test or a valuation` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 396(2) the evidence is proof of a fraudulent intent to affect the result of an assay, a test or a valuation` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 396(2) the evidence is proof of a fraudulent intent to affect the result of an assay, a test or a valuation` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `the prohibitions as regulative rules (SHANT): doing the act is the breach`
#TRACE `s 394(1) the prohibition on the person` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 394(1) defraud or conceal as the holder of a lease or licence` AT 1
#TRACE `s 394(2) the prohibition on the person` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 394(2) sell an unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed valuable mineral` AT 1
#TRACE `s 394(3) the prohibition on the person` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
#TRACE `s 394(3) the prohibition on the person` NOTHING AT 0 WITH
#TRACE `s 394.1(1) the prohibition on the person` (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the accused` DOES `s 394.1(1) possess an unrefined, partly refined, uncut or otherwise unprocessed valuable mineral that has been stolen or dealt with contrary to section 394` AT 1
